---
import Copy from '../components/Copy.astro';
import ForMacs from '../components/ForMacs.astro';
import Loop from '../components/Loop.astro';
import NotchDemo from '../components/NotchDemo.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { latestRelease } from '../lib/release';

const release = await latestRelease();
const brew = 'brew install lorcanchinnock/tap/warble';
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <NotchDemo />
      <h1>Your music, in the notch</h1>
      <p class="lede">Warble shows what's playing in your Mac's notch. Hover over it to see the song, then play, pause, skip or switch speakers. When nothing's playing, it stays out of sight.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="button big" href="/download">Download Warble</a>
        <Copy command={brew} />
      </div>
      <ForMacs />
      <p class="meta">Free and open source. Beta {release.version}, for macOS 15 or later, on Apple silicon or Intel. <a href="#install">How to install</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="clips" aria-labelledby="clips">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="clips" class="visually-hidden">Warble in use</h2>
      <ul class="grid">
        <li class="card">
          <Loop name="rest" label="The notch at rest, with the album art on one side and a few moving bars on the other" />
          <p>At rest, the album art and a few moving bars.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <Loop name="hover" label="Hovering over the notch, which opens to the song, a progress bar and the controls" />
          <p>Hover over it to see the song.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <Loop name="skip" label="Clicking skip in the open notch, which changes to the next song" />
          <p>Skip a song without leaving what you're doing.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <Loop name="idle" label="Pausing a song, the notch going quiet after a few seconds, then hovering to see the last song played" />
          <p>Pause, and the notch goes quiet. Hover to play the last song again.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="points" aria-labelledby="points">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="points" class="visually-hidden">What Warble does</h2>
      <ul class="grid">
        <li class="card">
          <h3>Calm by default</h3>
          <p>When nothing's playing, Warble draws nothing and uses no CPU. A paused song stays for 10 seconds, then the notch is just a notch again. Extras, like a message when the track changes, start switched off.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3>Quick</h3>
          <p>A hover opens the player in a quarter of a second, and a click opens it at once. Play and pause change the moment you click, without waiting for the app to catch up.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3>Any player</h3>
          <p>Apple Music, Spotify, podcast apps, and video in Safari, Chrome or any other browser. If something stops Warble seeing what's playing, a small <b>!</b> beside the notch says why and how to fix it.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3>Every Mac</h3>
          <p>On a Mac without a notch, or a MacBook with its lid closed, Warble draws a notch of its own at the top of the screen. You choose which displays get one.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3>Private</h3>
          <p>No account, no cloud, no analytics. Warble only goes online to check for updates, which it asks about first.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3>Free</h3>
          <p>Free and open source, with no ads. The <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/warble">code is on GitHub</a>. If you like it, you can <a href="/sponsor">sponsor it</a>, which helps pay to have Apple notarize it.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="install" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <div class="wrap narrow-text">
      <h2 id="install-title">Install</h2>
      <Copy command={brew} />
      <p>Or <a href="/download">download the zip</a> and drag Warble into Applications.</p>
      <ForMacs />
      <p>Warble isn't notarized by Apple yet, so macOS blocks it the first time you open it:</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>Open Warble from Applications. macOS says it can't check Warble. Click <b>Done</b>.</li>
        <li>Open <b>System Settings</b>, choose <b>Privacy &amp; Security</b> and scroll down to <b>Security</b>.</li>
        <li>Click <b>Open Anyway</b> next to the message about Warble, then confirm.</li>
        <li>Play something. The notch slides out to show it.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Warble is a beta, still being built, so expect changes between versions. The <a href="/docs/get-started/">guide</a> covers the rest, and the <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/warble/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md">roadmap</a> lists what's coming.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(24px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .hero .wrap { justify-items: center; text-align: center; }
  .hero :global(.screen) { margin-bottom: clamp(4px, 2vw, 16px); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(40px, 6.5vw, 72px); margin: 0; }
  .lede { font-size: clamp(18px, 2.1vw, 21px); margin: 0; max-width: 32em; }
  .cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px 16px; justify-content: center; align-items: center; width: 100%; }
  .cta :global(.copy) { flex: 0 1 480px; min-width: 0; text-align: start; }
  .button.big { min-height: 50px; padding: 12px 24px; font-size: 17px; }
  .meta { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--secondary); max-width: 32em; }
  .meta a { color: var(--fg); }
  .hero :global(.for-macs) { justify-content: center; }

  section { padding-block: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .wrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; }

  .clips .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 420px), 1fr)); }
  .clips .card { padding: 6px 6px 16px; display: grid; gap: 12px; overflow: hidden; }
  .clips p { margin: 0; padding-inline: 18px; color: var(--secondary); }
  .clips :global(video) { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: calc(var(--radius) - 6px); display: block; }

  .grid { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--gap); grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 300px), 1fr)); }
  .grid .card { padding: 22px 24px; display: grid; gap: 8px; align-content: start; }
  .grid h3 { font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .grid p { margin: 0; color: var(--secondary); }
  .grid a { color: var(--fg); }

  .narrow-text { max-width: 640px; }
  .install h2 { font-size: clamp(30px, 4.5vw, 44px); }
  .install p { margin: 0; }
  .install a { color: var(--fg); }
  .steps { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.4em; display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .steps li::marker { color: var(--secondary); }

  .visually-hidden { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
